pokeplatinum-route.patch (tools/pokeplat_gen.py applies the patches in name order): the route pilot's Gen 4 frame hook (tools/route.py pt, docs/port-worker.md "Routes"): one call per field frame, after the
frame's field task and processes, into port/game/route_gen4.c (PortRoute4_Frame: the pilot's PortRouteState, the map
adapter). Test-only: the pilot does nothing unless its environment variables are set. Game behaviour and the DS build are
unchanged (the call is the port's). The start menu (start_menu.c StartMenu_Main: PortRoute4_StartMenu each frame), the
script's yes/no (scrcmd.c ScriptContext_WaitForYesNoResult: PortRoute4_YesNo) and the save's write (ScrCmd_TrySaveGame:
PortRoute4_Saved) tell the pilot's S, Py and Pn the menu's state (docs/platinum.md "Route chain"). The battle's
player menus (battle/battle_display.c: the action menu, the move menu, the yes/no, the forget-a-move screen) call
PortRoute4_BattleMenu each frame they wait and PortRoute4_BattleMove with the move menu's answer (the battle pilot).
battle_subscreen.c BattleSystem_Cursor_Battler (the double battle's target menu, cursor shown at the first key press) asks
PortRoute4_TargetCursorKeep before it restores the saved cursor position: with the pilot on, a saved button whose Pokemon has
fainted (blank, A does nothing on it) is not restored; the cursor starts where the game puts it with no saved position.
The test cheats (docs/platinum.md "Test cheats"; nothing changes unless BWPORT_TESTCHEAT=win / BWPORT_NOENCOUNTER=1):
battle_lib.c BattleSystem_CompareBattlerSpeed passes the turn order's speeds through PortRoute4_CheatSpeed,
battle_controller_player.c asks PortRoute4_CheatSide in DecrementPP (no PP used) and CheckMoveHitAccuracy (always hits)
and PortRoute4_CheatDamage in UpdateHP (the hit's damage); battle_script.c BtlCmd_UpdateHealthBar and
BtlCmd_UpdateHealthBarValue pass hpCalcTemp through PortRoute4_CheatHpCalc (the player's side's HP loss a script applies:
burn, poison, weather, Leech Seed, Curse, recoil, Spikes); field_control.c Field_CheckWildEncounter asks
PortRoute4_NoEncounter (no wild encounter on a step).
The party "knows" the field moves under the test cheat (BWPORT_TESTCHEAT=win; docs/platinum.md "Test cheats"): scrcmd_party.c
ScrCmd_FindPartySlotWithMove (every field move script: Cut, Rock Smash, Strength, Rock Climb, Surf, Defog, Waterfall) and
unk_02054884.c Party_HasMonWithMove (the field's Surf and Waterfall checks, field_control.c) answer slot 0 for those moves
when PortRoute4_CheatFieldMove says so (port/game/route_gen4.c); the badge checks stay real.
The deep-mud task (overlay005/ov5_021DFB54.c FieldTask_StuckInDeepMud, which ends only after five direction changes) calls
PortRoute4_DeepMud each frame it runs, so the pilot presses turns until it ends (port/game/route_gen4.c; docs/platinum.md).
overlay006/wild_encounters.c WildEncounters_TryMudEncounter (the mud tile's own encounter roll) asks PortRoute4_NoEncounter too.
